{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"gpt-oss-120b","context":"## Programmatic Access\n\nUse the following model IDs and endpoint URLs to access this model programmatically. For more information about the available APIs and endpoints, see APIs supported and Endpoints supported.\n\n| **Endpoint** | **Model ID** | **In-Region endpoint URL** | **Geo inference ID** | **Global inference ID** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `bedrock-runtime` | `openai.gpt-oss-120b-1:0` | `https://bedrock-runtime.{region}.amazonaws.com` | `us-gov.openai.gpt-oss-120b-1:0` | Not supported |\n| `bedrock-mantle` | `openai.gpt-oss-120b` | `https://bedrock-mantle.{region}.api.aws/v1` | Not supported | Not supported |\n\n*For example, if region is us-east-1 (N. Virginia), then the bedrock-runtime endpoint URL will be \"https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-1.amazonaws.com\" and for bedrock-mantle will be \"https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-1.api.aws/v1\".*","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-openai-gpt-oss-120b.html"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"GPT-5.5","context":"## Programmatic Access\n\nUse the following model IDs and endpoint URLs to access this model programmatically. For more information about the available APIs and endpoints, see APIs supported and Endpoints supported.\n\n| **Endpoint** | **Model ID** | **In-Region endpoint URL** | **Geo inference ID** | **Global inference ID** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `bedrock-runtime` | `openai.gpt-5.5` | Not supported | `us.openai.gpt-5.5` | `global.openai.gpt-5.5` |\n| `bedrock-mantle` | `openai.gpt-5.5` | `https://bedrock-mantle.{region}.api.aws/openai/v1` | Not supported | Not supported |\n\n*For example, if region is us-east-1 (N. Virginia), then the bedrock-mantle endpoint URL will be \"https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-1.api.aws/openai/v1\". On `bedrock-runtime`, the base URL is \"https://bedrock-runtime.{region}.amazonaws.com/openai/v1\" and requests must name a cross-Region inference ID — `us.openai.gpt-5.5` or `global.openai.gpt-5.5` — as the model.*","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-openai-gpt-55.html"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Introducing Gemma 4 models on Amazon Bedrock | Artificial Intelligence","context":"## Accessing Gemma 4 models on Amazon Bedrock\n\nYou access Gemma 4 models on Amazon Bedrock through the `bedrock-mantle` endpoint, the OpenAI-compatible API purpose-built for the next-generation inference engine for Amazon Bedrock. Its endpoint URL is `https://bedrock-mantle.{region}.api.aws/openai/v1`, and it exposes the Chat Completions and Responses APIs.\n\nIt’s helpful to keep the endpoint and the engine distinct: the *engine* is the underlying serving infrastructure—designed with Model Deployment Account isolation and zero operator access—and the *endpoint* is the HTTPS API surface you call. The `bedrock-mantle` endpoint is the public API for that next-generation inference engine and exposes its full feature set. For a deeper look at the underlying inference engine, refer to Exploring the zero operator access design of Amazon Bedrock’s next-generation inference engine.\n\nThe `bedrock-mantle` endpoint uses the same interface as the OpenAI Python and TypeScript SDKs, so teams already on those SDKs can switch to Gemma 4 models on Amazon Bedrock by updating only the base URL and model ID. It also supports Amazon Bedrock API keys, projects, and client-side tool calling","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/introducing-gemma-4-models-on-amazon-bedrock/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"Gemma 4 31B","context":"## Programmatic Access\n\nUse the following model IDs and endpoint URLs to access this model programmatically. For more information about the available APIs and endpoints, see APIs supported and Endpoints supported.\n\n| **Endpoint** | **Model ID** | **In-Region endpoint URL** | **Geo inference ID** | **Global inference ID** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `bedrock-mantle` | `google.gemma-4-31b` | `https://bedrock-mantle.{region}.api.aws/openai/v1` | Not supported | Not supported |\n\n*For example, if region is us-east-1 (N. Virginia), then the bedrock-mantle endpoint URL will be \"https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-1.api.aws/openai/v1\".*","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-google-gemma-4-31b.html"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"Gemma 4 26B-A4B","context":"## Programmatic Access\n\nUse the following model IDs and endpoint URLs to access this model programmatically. For more information about the available APIs and endpoints, see APIs supported and Endpoints supported.\n\n| **Endpoint** | **Model ID** | **In-Region endpoint URL** | **Geo inference ID** | **Global inference ID** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `bedrock-mantle` | `google.gemma-4-26b-a4b` | `https://bedrock-mantle.{region}.api.aws/openai/v1` | Not supported | Not supported |\n\n*For example, if region is us-east-1 (N. Virginia), then the bedrock-mantle endpoint URL will be \"https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-1.api.aws/openai/v1\".*","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-card-google-gemma-4-26b-a4b.html"}]}}

