{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Amazon Bedrock adds support for the latest open-weight models in Asia Pacific (Sydney) - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock, a managed service offering secure access to high-performance foundation models from leading AI companies, has announced support for the latest open-weight models in Asia Pacific (Sydney) via the bedrock-mantle endpoint. The endpoint is powered by Project Mantle, a new distributed inference engine for large-scale machine learning model serving on Amazon Bedrock. Supported providers include DeepSeek, Google, MiniMax, Mistral, Moonshot AI, Nvidia, and OpenAI. Project Mantle simplifies model onboarding, provides performant and reliable serverless inference, offers sophisticated quality of service controls, and delivers OpenAI API compatibility out-of-the-box. To learn more and get started, visit the Amazon Bedrock console or service documentation, and for OpenAI API-compatible service endpoints, refer to the OpenAI API compatibility documentation","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/amazon-bedrock-support-latest-open-weight-models-asia-pacific-sydney/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Amazon Bedrock expands API support and introduces Cross Region Inferencing for OpenAI models - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock has expanded its API support to include OpenAI GPT-5.6 models (Sol, Terra, and Luna) on the bedrock-runtime endpoint, with compatibility for the Responses, Converse, and Chat Completions APIs. The update introduces cross-region inference, allowing customers to access higher throughput and lower inference costs by automatically routing requests across multiple AWS Regions. Geo cross-region inference keeps data processed within a specific geography, while Global cross-region inference serves requests from any commercial AWS Region where the model is available. This launch also expands API support for OpenAI models, enabling usage of the Responses API, Chat Completions API, and Converse API on the bedrock-runtime endpoint. Cross-region inference for OpenAI models is now available in all AWS Regions where OpenAI models on Amazon Bedrock are offered. Usage is logged and can be attributed to model invocation logging, Amazon CloudWatch metrics, AWS Cost Explorer, and the AWS Cost and Usage Report. Cross-region inference for OpenAI models is available in all AWS Regions where OpenAI models on Amazon Bedrock are offered. To get started, review the model cards for GPT 5.6 (Sol, Tera, and Luna) in the Amazon Bedrock User Guide","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/08/amazon-bedrock-cross-region-openai-v2/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Amazon Bedrock announces OpenAI-compatible Projects API - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock, a fully managed AI service, has introduced OpenAI-compatible Projects API support in its Mantle inference engine. This update enables users with multiple applications, environments, or teams to create individual projects for better isolation. Each project can have distinct IAM-based access control and tags for enhanced cost visibility. The Projects API is accessible to all customers using OpenAI-compatible APIs, including the Responses API and Chat Completions API, through Mantle inference engine in Amazon Bedrock. There is no extra charge for utilizing the Projects API; users only pay for the underlying model inference consumption. To initiate using the Projects API in Amazon Bedrock, refer to the Amazon Bedrock documentation","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/03/amazon-bedrock-projects-api-mantle-inference-engine/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"amazon-bedrock","skill_description":"Builds generative AI applications on Amazon Bedrock. Covers model invocation (Converse API, InvokeModel), RAG with Knowledge Bases, Bedrock Agents, Guardrails, and AgentCore (including the Harness managed agent loop). Applies when invoking models, setting up or migrating Knowledge Bases to Managed, deploying to AgentCore, migrating/porting/converting a Bedrock Agent (including inline agents) to an AgentCore Harness, troubleshooting Bedrock errors (ThrottlingException, AccessDeniedException), or choosing Bedrock models (Claude, Llama, Nova, Titan). Also for prompt caching, quota and throttling diagnosis, cost tracking, migrating between Claude model generations, chunking strategies, and Bedrock model selection. Covers AgentCore Payments (x402, microtransactions, Payment Manager, Connector, Instrument, Coinbase CDP, Stripe Privy, paid endpoints, agent payments). NOT for custom model training, Rekognition, or Comprehend. For SageMaker model discovery, customization, or endpoints, use aws-ai-ml.\n\nServices: bedrock, bedrock-runtime, bedrock-mantle, bedrock-agent, bedrock-agent-runtime, bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, design, migrate\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: generative-ai, rag, agents","skill_name":"amazon-bedrock"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"aws-ai-ml","skill_description":"Selects, deploys, and customizes AI models on Amazon SageMaker. Training or Processing jobs, fine-tuning (SFT/DPO/RLVR/RLAIF), model selection, evaluation, SageMaker or Bedrock deployment, inference optimization and endpoint diagnostics. Use when fine-tuning models on SageMaker, choosing a base model to customize or deploy from SageMaker JumpStart or Hub, SageMakerPublicHub, or the model catalog, checking data quality (duplicates, languages, PII), transforming or validating data (reformat, clean, filter, dedupe, split, merge, redact), generating synthetic data, labeling data with a model, human review or annotation and applying its corrections, evaluating model quality, deploying or optimizing endpoints, configuring IAM/S3, or managing SageMaker Managed MLflow. Use for endpoint health, latency, logs, metrics, errors. Covers Serverless Model Customization, Nova and OSS deployment paths, and PySDK v3. NOT for SageMaker Ground Truth labeling jobs, Feature Store, or general AWS infrastructure.\n\nServices: sagemaker, s3, iam, bedrock\nTasks: build, deploy, debug, optimize\nPersona: developer, data-scientist\nWorkload: ai-ml","skill_name":"aws-ai-ml"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search docs for the Bedrock Mantle endpoint and supported models"}
